  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="90dda084-3359-5db0-b7c1-85301e50ffa7" activityNameId="a86dc8b6-660d-52ab-9a18-2fea1bbddfdc" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">xx Lead, secondary, from electronic and electric scrap recycling, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: xx Lead, secondary, from electronic and electric scrap recycling, at plant
The multi-output-process "secondary copper conversion" delivers the co-products "metal values from electric waste, in blister-copper, at converter" and "lead, secondary, from electronic and electric scrap recycling, at plant". The product "metal values from electric waste, …" is an intermediary in the production of secondary gold from electric scrap and is not to be used by the LCA practitioner.  The flow "lead, …" is a by-product of this process that receives part of the burdens allocated. It must not be used to reflect lead.;
UUID: ceb8aefd-b53f-3d2a-a5e2-57dd8e57af7d
Inculdes the processing of e-scrap in the Boliden process by the Kaldo plant and the converter aisle.
Location: Data describes a Swedish plant that is singular in the region and ranges worldwide among the big producer. It may be taken as approximation for the global situation
Technology: Conversion of Copper in a Kaldo Converter and treatment in converter aisle.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: Literature 
Extrapolations: see Geography and Technology
Uncertainty adjustments: see Geography and Technology
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_ceb8aefd-b53f-3d2a-a5e2-57dd8e57af7d.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
